{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>ואשתדור</b> — Targum: 'here I have sent this kid.' שדרית: emissaries would bring gifts near to those who aided them. עלילות as in 'he was dispatched to his Excellency.'"], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The word עלילות (literally 'example' or 'allusion') here functions as Ibn Ezra's equivalent of 'e.g.' or 'as in,' introducing an illustration; the phrase הוה משתדר להצלותיה ('he was dispatched to his Excellency') is likely a quotation or near-quotation illustrating the Aramaic root שדר in correspondence contexts. The syntax of the final clause is compressed and somewhat elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:55.988431202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}